WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.899
It can’t be easy to keep secrets for a movie
as big — and exciting — as Avengers 4,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.760
but these actors probably could have tried
a little harder.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.240
These are a few of the biggest slip-ups by
the leading lights of the MCU.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.180
A tiny detail

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.351
There’s been plenty of speculation that
the Quantum Realm will come into play in a

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:21.710
major way in Avengers 4 — and it looks like
Tom Holland may have confirmed that this is

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:22.200
the case.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.140
Speaking with Benedict Cumberbatch in a video
released by Emergency Awesome, Holland referenced

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:31.640
the Quantum Realm specifically when comparing
his dialogue in Avengers 4 to Cumberbatch's.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.560
“He has to talk about so much quantum realm stuff.. just stuff.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.180
"I just have to say 'this is awesome.   this is cool!”

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.220
Unless the dialogue Holland is referring to
is along the lines of, "Gee, I'm relieved

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.280
we don't have to deal with any of that dumb
Quantum Realm stuff," then it's a safe bet

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.190
the strange place Scott Lang is trapped in
is going to hold some importance in the final

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.340
battle against Thanos.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.220
Long live the Queen

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.079
While promoting Mission: Impossible – Fallout,
Angela Bassett — who played T'Challa's mother

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:05.440
Ramonda in Black Panther — revealed to ScreenRant
that Ramonda and Shuri survived Thanos' purge

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.380
at the end of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.180
When asked if her character was killed, Bassett
replied:

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.020
"No.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.020
Neither did my daughter.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.860
Shuri, she's a bright girl there in Wakanda."

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.500
The fact that both characters survived could
have a serious impact on the story of Avengers

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.500
4 and beyond.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.700
On the one hand, with T'Challa dead, the survival
of Shuri and Ramonda may help determine who

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.620
takes the throne.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.900
On the other, when last we saw Shuri, she
was trying to separate the Mind Stone from

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.450
Vision without killing him; she didn't succeed,
but she still might have gained valuable knowledge

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:37.220
which our heroes could use in the coming battle
against Thanos.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.120
The women of Marvel

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.090
In an interview with Paper Magazine, Pom Klementieff
— who plays Mantis in the Guardians films

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.869
and Infinity War — was asked about the #MeToo
movement, and her response may have unintentionally

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:52.580
revealed a team-up between Mantis, Captain
Marvel and Okoye.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.560
She recalled:

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.100
"I remember Brie Larson coming to me and Danai
Gurira [ on the set of

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.640
The Avengers.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.440
She told me about the [Time's Up] letter to
sign and I found it really amazing to have

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.200
all these women — and men too — together
in fighting for a better world."

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.349
Mantis may have been one of the victims of
Thanos' purge at the end of Avengers: Infinity

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:13.169
War, but Klementieff's words would imply that
her death won't be entirely permanent.

00:02:13.169 --> 00:02:17.340
And if we're getting a team-up between those
three, it begs the question of just where

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:17.840
it's happening.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:22.500
Have Mantis and Captain Marvel made their
way to Earth, or is Okoye somehow traveling

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.480
the stars?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:24.960
Reunited

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.860
Since Avengers 4 promises to be Robert Downey
Jr.'s final work in the MCU, fans wouldn't

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.999
be blamed for assuming Tony Stark might not
survive to see Pepper Potts again.

00:02:34.999 --> 00:02:39.090
Tony was already a top choice for the Avengers:
Infinity War kill list and it's a good bet

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.400
the stakes will be raised even higher for
Avengers 4.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.029
Thanks to Gwyneth Paltrow's Instagram page,
however, we know Tony and Pepper will get

00:02:46.029 --> 00:02:47.800
to see each other at least one more time.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.120
“I’m sorry."

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.260
In September 2018, while Avengers 4 was in
the middle of reshoots, Paltrow posted a photo

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.580
of her and Downey on set.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:08.780
The caption read simply "lunchtime", accompanied
by "#pepperony," — a mash-up of Pepper and

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.280
Tony.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.860
So we may not know whether Pepper or Tony
will survive Avengers 4, but we do know that

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.640
their scene in Infinity War wasn't the last
time the pair would see each other.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.260
The good old days

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:24.969
The same day Gwyneth Paltrow posted her "#pepperony"
shot on Instagram, Chris Evans posted a selfie

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:29.920
on Twitter unveiling a relatively minor spoiler
to eagle-eyed fans — but one that could

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.820
point to a much larger reveal.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.779
In the photo, Evans' Infinity War facial hair
is gone and his hair more closely resembles

00:03:36.779 --> 00:03:38.969
the look we've seen in earlier films.

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:42.959
The shot's caption reads "Senior Year" and
is followed by "#A4."

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:47.370
As Thor correctly pointed out during Infinity
War's Battle of Wakanda, the star-spangled

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.320
Avenger assumed a much scruffier look in Infinity
War.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.300
“New haircut?"

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.600
"Notice you've copied my beard!"

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.180
Now, this photo could simply mean that by
the end of Avengers 4 Steve Rogers will decide

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.200
he's not keen on beards anymore.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.519
However, the idea that the Avengers will be
bouncing around time is one of the more heavily

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.600
trafficked theories about Avengers 4.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.280
Evans could easily have been involved in reshoots
for a scene involving a Captain America from

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.060
another era.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.880
In particular, the photo gives credence to
a fan theory that was already growing in popularity

00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:25.840
— that Captain America will not die in Avengers
4, but will instead be sent back in time to

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.240
live the life with Peggy Carter that his long
sleep in the ice stole from him.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:32.560
If true, it could be a beautiful end to the
character's story.

